==Old English==

===Etymology===
''Tiwes'' (''genitive'' of [[Tiw|Tīw]]) + [[dæg|dæġ]]. Cognate with Old Frisian ''Tiesdei'', Old High German ''zīostag'' (dialectal German ''Zistig''), Old Norse ''týrsdagr'' (Swedish ''[[tisdag]]''). Used in translation of the Latin ''[[dies Martis]]''

